Z||000003||Cheever3000||11-24-2001||03:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by maryjane:<BR><B>Cheever, I take it your family were safe? Kinda left us hangin unless I missed it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Long story...<BR>The above post was for showing SpeedRacer how to post pics.  He & his dad came down from Kansas to buy a Fiero they saw on eBay (which turned out to be a mistake - I'll let him tell about it) then they dropped by my house for a fastback clip.  Anyway, they arrived just as my parents were leaving to go back to Tulsa, chauffered (sp?) by my brother who flew here for the purpose of getting them back safely.<P>Okay, so what happened was:<BR>They didn't show up Tuesday night.  Wednesday about noon we told the state police they were overdue.  At work Wed night I got a call that they were found in Port Gibson, Mississippi (!!!).  A sheriff's dept lady officer saw Dad walking around the van inspecting it for damage after hitting a curb (somehow he imagined it had a lot of damage but it had none).  She asked some questions and could tell they didn't know where they were.  She got enough info to call a relative who called us.  The officer made them think the van would be in a shop overnight getting fixed, and put them up in the local hospital - this was just to give us time to get there.  So we were there when they awoke Thursday morning.  Dad wondered how the van was "fixed" so quickly, but we drove them to my house for a late Thanksgiving dinner.  A few calls to my brother in Tulsa, and he got a plane ticket to come & drive them home.  They'll be fine in their familiar surroundings, but we're going to try to get them both to a doctor.  I was able to convince them of where they were found (they didn't believe it at first), but they have no idea how they got there or what they did during 24 hours to complete a 10-12 hour drive and still not ending up anywhere close to our house.  We may never know.<P>||||reg||1
